  "reason": "The standout result is config_007 (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.635), which dramatically outperforms config_018 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.542) with only the RNA encoder changed. This strongly implicates the RNA encoder as the critical design choice. The key uncertainty is whether the pca_n2000 advantage is specific to the imagenet_vit_l image encoder or generalizes. config_004 (pca_n2000 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted) is a single-variable change from config_007 (image encoder swap) and from config_002 (scgpt + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.525; RNA encoder swap). One experiment thus yields two clean comparisons: (a) RNA encoder effect with resnet50 (config_004 vs config_002) and (b) image encoder effect with pca_n2000 (config_004 vs config_007). Under a limited budget, confirming whether the dominant pca_n2000 signal is robust across image encoders is the highest-value uncertainty to resolve before investing further in aggregation or fusion variations."
}

